      "evidence": "Skip to Main Content\nEvents\nSearchSign InSign In\nMore\nHostsOpenAI & Cerebral Valley\nGPT-6 Astra Hackathon SF\nSan Francisco, CATue, Sep 8 at 9:00 AM – 10:00 PM (PDT)\n\nGPT-6 Astra is here. Come build with it.\n\nThis hackathon is for developers, technical founders, and startup teams to build with GPT-6 Astra – the world’s most intelligent and aligned model. Meet the OpenAI team and compete for a chance to demo onstage for a panel of judges including Urvashi Barooah (Redpoint), Pranav Reddy (Conviction), Romain Huet (OpenAI), swyx (AIE), and Lan Xuezhao (Basis Set)! \n\nPrizes:\n\n1st place - $50,000 credits + DevDay 2026 tickets\n2nd place - $25,000 credits\n3rd place - $15,000 credits\nAll finalists - 1 year of ChatGPT Pro\n\nRules:\n\nShow us what you can ship with GPT-6 Astra's new capabilities, whether that’s something new or a feature for your existing startup. All work must be built during the hackathon and submitted as a public open source repository - existing product code does not qualify.\n\nApplications reviewed on a rolling basis & space is limited. Maximum teams of four. All attendees must submit an application to be approved.\n\nPlease note: This event is fully in-person in San Francisco. Capacity is limited. Teams may have up to four members. All attendees must apply and be approved. Submitting an application does not guarantee a seat; approved applicants must confirm their attendance.\n\nJoin Waitlist",
